// Spec §2.1, §14.1 — partner application status lifecycle.
// Spec canonical English names → DB stored values (@map) → Bulgarian display labels:
//   NEW          → "NOVA"          → Нова
//   COMMUNICATION→ "KOMUNIKACIYA"  → Комуникация
//   NEGOTIATION  → "DOGOVARYANE"   → Договаряне
//   ONBOARDING   → "ONBOARDING"    → Онбординг
//   APPROVED     → "ODOBRENA"      → Одобрена
//   REJECTED     → "OTKAZANA"      → Отказана
//
// The @map directives preserve the Bulgarian-transliterated DB column values
// that exist in production rows while exposing spec-canonical English Prisma
// enum names to all application code. Any code checking a request status MUST
// use the enum constant (e.g. PartnerRequestStatus.NEW), never the raw string.
enum PartnerRequestStatus {
  NEW           @map("NOVA")
  COMMUNICATION @map("KOMUNIKACIYA")
  NEGOTIATION   @map("DOGOVARYANE")
  ONBOARDING    @map("ONBOARDING")
  APPROVED      @map("ODOBRENA")
  REJECTED      @map("OTKAZANA")
}

// Spec §1.1 defines exactly three canonical partner_account_status values:
// Active | Inactive | Archived.
//
// This enum intentionally carries SEVEN values, not three. The four extra values
// (PENDING, SUSPENDED, PAUSED, REJECTED) are INTERNAL operational sub-states; they
// are retained for fine-grained status history and backwards compatibility and are
// NOT part of the partner-facing API contract. All seven values MUST be normalized
// onto the canonical three (Active | Inactive | Archived) at the partner-facing API
// boundary per the mapping table at the bottom of this comment. Do NOT remove any
// enum value (existing production rows depend on them).
//
// PAUSED and SUSPENDED are extended operational sub-states retained in this
// schema for fine-grained status history and backwards compatibility.
// ALL code MUST normalize them to INACTIVE before any partner-facing API
// response leaves the server. This includes:
//   - Profile endpoints (partner portal, public profile)
//   - Auth token payload / JWT claims
//   - Status change notification payloads (PARTNER_STATUS_CHANGE)
//   - QR cascade logic (treat PAUSED/SUSPENDED as non-ACTIVE)
//   - Public-visibility gate (treat PAUSED/SUSPENDED as non-ACTIVE)
//   - Login gate (treat PAUSED/SUSPENDED as blocked — no portal access)
//   - Any query filtering by status MUST include PAUSED and SUSPENDED
//     whenever the intent is to match all "Inactive" partners. Using a
//     simple WHERE status='INACTIVE' will silently miss these rows.
//
// Use the Partner.statusReason field to carry the sub-classification
// (e.g. "VOLUNTARY_PAUSE" | "ADMIN_SUSPENSION" | "FAILED_PAYMENT_SUSPENSION")
// so the display layer can show the Bulgarian label (Пауза vs Спрян) without
// extending the external API contract.
//
// PENDING: pre-activation state (partner applied but activation link not yet
//   consumed). Treated as non-operational in QR, visibility, and login gates.
//   Treat identically to ARCHIVED for access control purposes.
//
// REJECTED: application was rejected at the pre-partner stage. Treated as
//   non-operational. Partners in REJECTED status cannot log in or access
//   the portal. NOTE: REJECTED as a partner_application_status (PartnerRequestStatus)
//   is semantically distinct — do not conflate the two.
//
// Canonical mapping table for all external-facing serializers:
//   ACTIVE    → "Active"
//   INACTIVE  → "Inactive"
//   PAUSED    → "Inactive"   (statusReason distinguishes from pure Inactive)
//   SUSPENDED → "Inactive"   (statusReason distinguishes from pure Inactive)
//   ARCHIVED  → "Archived"
//   PENDING   → not surfaced externally (treat as "Inactive" / blocked)
//   REJECTED  → not surfaced externally (treat as "Inactive" / blocked)
enum PartnerStatus {
  PENDING
  ACTIVE
  SUSPENDED
  INACTIVE
  PAUSED
  ARCHIVED
  REJECTED
}

